  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Once dates are booked, members can update an attendance sheet before each rehearsal, and the conductor can inspect it while preparing.\", \"decision\": \"How should expected attendance reach the conductor?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nSection leaders ask their singers about the next rehearsal and enter section totals on the attendance sheet. A short personal check produces a useful picture of balance without requiring the conductor to chase individual replies.\nMembers mark their expected attendance on the shared sheet by the day before each rehearsal. The conductor sees individual updates in one place and can anticipate missing voices before choosing the session’s emphasis.\nThe organizer sends a rehearsal reminder with an attendance response link and summarizes replies for the conductor. Confirmation is prompted at a predictable time, making the expected numbers easier to use during final preparation."
    }
  ],
